From a3ac376d44f0b7a57186f826598dd6b59295db59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:13:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] drm: apple: Drive the T8122 dcpext through the 14.7
 IOMFB template

Aurora accepts 14.7 firmware only for processors that the boot loader
hands over (T6030, the J613 panel) and drives them through its DCPLink
session. The T8122 dcpext is not handed over: Linux starts it, as on
M1/M2. asahi-wip-7.2 with AsahiLinux/linux#607 drives this dcpext with
14.7 firmware through the classic IOMFB template.

Add that path, for apple,t8122-dcpext only:
- iomfb_v14_7_tpl.c: the asahi-wip-7.2 14.7 method and callback tables
  around the shared template (symbols *_v14_7_0, no clash with Aurora's
  iomfb_v14_7_*);
- DCP_FIRMWARE_V_14_7_TEMPLATE, selected by dcp_check_firmware_version()
  for apple,t8122-dcpext with firmware-compat 14.7.0, and dispatched like
  12.3/13.5 (component bind, RTKit boot, dcp_start endpoints, template
  modeset/flush/power), so that every path that tests
  DCP_FIRMWARE_V_14_7 (the DCPLink session, T6030) is left alone;
- dcp_fw_is_14_7() for the firmware protocol of the AFK, DPTX and DPAV
  endpoints, which both paths share; external backlight levels stay off
  on 14.7 either way;
- the plane id as surface id in swaps, as asahi-wip-7.2 does for 14.7;
- an apple,t8122-dcpext match entry (2 DPTX ports, as generic dcpext);
- AFK: after START_ENDPOINT give the firmware 10 ms to set the endpoint
  up, and poll the mailbox while waiting for the init acknowledgment,
  because the ASC of a freshly booted processor can leave messages
  queued without another recv-not-empty interrupt.

The internal panel (apple,t8122-dcp, DCP_FIRMWARE_V_14_7) and every
other processor are unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/linux/pull/607
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
